EXTENSION "ARMDef_Dies_Irae_TheTwilightOfTheGods_QualitiesAndUtiseta" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Dies Irae - Chapter Five: The Twilight of the Gods qualities and utiseta"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-08"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Dies_Irae_Core_Ext"

    # The chapter's qualities and utiseta, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.

    #tfa12d6eb97c5a5dc7274ea ^"The Snatcher of the Moon" DEF {
        EXTENDS #ta802193baa1091f6e9f4ee ^"Utiseta"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ability" STRING "Sjonhverfing"
            ^"Ease Factor" INTEGER 48
            ^"Range" STRING "Sight"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Decade"
            ^"Target" STRING "Boundary"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 12, +9 Sight, +15 Decade, +12 Boundary)"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "Sjonhverfing Ease Factor 48 R: Sight, D: Decade, T: Boundary"
            ^"Source" STRING "Dies Irae"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 133
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This *utiseta* creates the image of a mighty wolf that seems to swallow the moon; from this day onwards, the moon is not seen for ten years. The illusion only holds when within the same geographical region as the Muspelli when the ritual was cast; if characters travel out of the region the moon reappears.\n\nTo complete this utiseta, a Muspelli with a good score in Sjonhverfing (7) would need Power Modifiers of x5 or x6. This would probably mean that they will be located on islands on lakes (sites symbolic to Fenrir) all over Mythic Europe, performing rites of self-mutilation and sacrifices of creatures with Faerie Might. These rituals would take an average of seven hours to complete. For more information on the Muspelli and their *utiseta* rituals, see *Rival Magic*, Chapter 4. While Muspelli cannot combine their powers, in this case they are simply creating multiple illusions from many different vantage points."
    }

}
